      <div type="clause" n="84">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 84</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="84" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="368" ed="#liebermann"/>Nu bidde ic georne — ⁊ on Godes naman beode — manna gehwylcne, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he inweardre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_84.lnote.oe.1-2"/> heortan gebuge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_84.lnote.oe.2-2"/> to his Drihtne ⁊ oft ⁊ gelome smeage<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_84.lnote.oe.3-2"/> swyðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_84.lnote.oe.4"/> georne, hwæt him sig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_84.lnote.oe.5"/> to donne ⁊ hwæt to forganne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="84" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="368" ed="#liebermann"/>Nu bidde ic georne — ⁊ on Godes naman beode — manna gehwylcne, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he inweardre heortan gebuga to his Drihtene ⁊ oft ⁊ gelome smeage, hwæt him sy to donne ⁊ hwæt to forganne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="84" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="368" ed="#liebermann"/>Nu bidde ic georne — ⁊ on Godes naman beode — manna gehwylcne, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he inweardlice<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_84.lnote.oe.1-3"/> heor<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_84.lnote.oe.2-3"/> gebuge to his Drihtne ⁊ oft ⁊ gelome smeage swiðe georne, hwæt him sy to donne ⁊ hwæt to forganne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="84" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="369" ed="#liebermann"/>Denique sedulo precor et in Dei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_84.lnote.oe.1"/> nomine precipio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_84.lnote.oe.2"/> omnibus hominibus, ut intimo corde conuertantur ad Deum et semper et assidue diligenter inquirant, quid eis sit agendum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_84.lnote.oe.3"/> (faciendum), quid uero dimittendum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="84" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="369" ed="#liebermann"/>Nunc uero precor diligenter et nomine Dei iubeo hominem quemque, ut intimo corde supplicet Deo suo et sepe et frequenter satagat diligenter, quid sibi sit faciendum, et quid omittendum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="84" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="216" ed="#robertson"/>Nu bidde ic georne ⁊ on Godes naman beode manna gehwylcne, þæt he inweardre<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#IICn_84.robnote.fn.6"/> heortan gebuga to his Drihtene, ⁊ oft ⁊ gelome smeage<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#IICn_84.robnote.fn.7"/> hwæt him sy to donne ⁊ hwæt to forganne.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="296" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Nu bidde ic georne and on Godes naman beode manna gehwylcne, þæt he inweardre heortan gebuge to his drihtne and oft and gelome smeage swyðe georne hwæt him sig to donne and hwæt to forganne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_84.lnote.de.1"/><pb n="369" ed="#liebermann"/>Nun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_84.lnote.de.2"/> bitte ich ernstlich — und gebiete in Gottes Namen — einem jeden der Menschen, dass er aus innerstem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_84.lnote.de.3"/> Herzen sich seinem Herrgott unterwerfe und oft und häufig recht ernsthaft nachdenke, was ihm zu thun und was zu unterlassen sei.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Now I earnestly beg — and command in God's name — each and every person that he submit himself with his inmost heart to his Lord God and often and frequently consider very earnestly what he should do and what he should refrain from.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_84.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="217" ed="#robertson"/>Now I earnestly entreat all men and command them, in the name of God, to submit in their inmost hearts to their lord, and often and frequently consider what they ought to do and what they ought to forgo.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="297" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Now in God’s name, I sincerely charge and command all the people to submit to their Lord in their innermost hearts and often and frequently reflect carefully upon what they should do and what they should forgo.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">A forgot ‘-tan’ at the beginning of the next line.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 369, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">swyðe georne: omitted B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">369</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">n. Dei <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">n. Dei Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">369</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o. h. p. <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> o. uobis p. <hi rend="italic">Co</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o. h. p. K; o. uobis p. Co</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">369</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ag. <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> f. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ag. K; f. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">inweardlice <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">inweardlice Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">buge <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">buge Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nochmals</hi> smeage, <hi rend="italic">aber ausradirt G</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">smeage again, but erased G</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">swiþe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">swiþe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">für</hi> -licre [<hi rend="italic">s. o. I</hi> 21]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">for -licre [see above I 21]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84.lnote.oe.2-3" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Zeilenende;</hi> tan <hi rend="italic">zu Beginn der folg. Zeile vergessen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">end of line; tan forgotten at the beginning of the next line</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_84.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dies Kapitel bildet den Epilog, lautet homiletisch und wiederholt mehrfach den Epilog zu I Cn, sowie Gedanken anderer Stellen in I Cn; <hi rend="italic">vgl</hi>. Einl. 17ff.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">This chapter forms the epilogue; it is homiletic in tone and repeats the epilogue to I Cn in several places, as well as ideas from other passages of I Cn; <hi rend="italic">cf</hi>. Introduction 17ff.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_84.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Z. T. derselbe Eingang I 7</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">In part the same opening I 7</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_84.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ebenso I 21</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Likewise I 21</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_84.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">With this clause and the next, cf. I Cn. 21.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_84.robnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">216</biblScope></bibl><label>inweardre</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">inweardlice</hi> A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_84.robnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">216</biblScope></bibl><label>smeage</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">sm. swyðe</hi> (<hi rend="italic">swiðe</hi>) <hi rend="italic">georne</hi> G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
